survey swil2b
#Data from Willie Stanton's Survey Book 1 
# p. 47-50	(=PDF p.51-54)

#Typed in by Footleg, June 2012

#5th August 1951	SWILDONS HOLE SURVEY
#Through Sump 1 to Swildons 2 streamway, start of 4 Letter Link and start of Approach Passage, 
#Swildons 2 streamway from Creep 2 to Sump 2, inlet from Landing to Muddy Sump

centreline
cs OSGB:ST 
date 1951.08.05
# Stanton's bearings come out 3 degrees clockwise of the resurvey even after
# the magnetic declination Therion works out for the date. Measured on his
# streamway books (swildons1-c, d and e, 1952-53) against the resurvey there,
# where it is the same for all three; assumed for his other books.
calibrate compass 3    # back bearings too

#in this survey some angles are in degrees:minutes, others decimal degrees
units tape feet
units depth feet

data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
C1	D1	11.8	-	85	-24	On rocky bank.
D1	A	36.8	251	-	0	D1 to near side of Sump I 11.8'. D1 to far side of Sump I 18'. D1 is in pool at stake for cable.
U	V	29	-	6:30	0	Lake begins as 10'. (Little sketch)
V	W	33.8	141:30	-	0	Lake
W	X	47	132:10	-	0	Bearing from 2' to right. W to near side Duck II = 3.5. W to far side Duck II = 20.4
data diving from to tape compass backcompass depthchange ignoreall						
X	Y	83.5	-	354	-0.7	Y at lip of Sump II, 3" air space goes on 10 more
data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
#	Y					(Little sketch). Total 1010'
T	Ri	22.1	19	-	20	
Ri	Rii	46	315	-	-3	Sump on left at 41' feet
Rii	Riii	32	348	-	2	Bearing from 3 feet to left
data diving from to tape compass backcompass depthchange ignoreall						
Riii	Riv	27.3	284	-	-4	Bearing from 2' to left. Iv is Muddy Sump. Dp below Sump I is 20.6 feet. Total 1127'
data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
a2	b2	43	83	-	15	a is on N.Side of passage just before Creep I -> (sketch)
b2	c2	20.7	6	-	8	
c2	d2	11.3	42	-	10	
d2	e2	18.9	139	-	0	(e) is where passage rejoins streamway. Stn 35 (p.52)-(e) is F.S. 234 (TRUE), Dist 18', Clino +45 (deg), HD 12.7, VD +12.7
d2	f2	10.3	245	-	60	
f2	g2	6.2	319	-	0	
g2	h2	16	237	-	65	
h2	i2	46	329	-	0	(i) is where passage gets too low. (some indistinct numbers follow. Too faint to read on logbook scan). Total 1207' (?)
M	1	11.7	-	145	-20	
1	2	28.5	35	-	85	
2	3	19.9	-	230	16	2 is on lip of Approach passage. Little passage starts 15 back.
3	4	16	122	-	7	3 - 12 Trench up to 2 feet deep in floor of this passage
4	5	18	59	-	15	Little passage off to South from 4
5	6	9.5	17	-	10	
6	7	13.5	46	-	17	
7	8	24.2	74	-	13	
8	9	8.8	137	-	10	
9	10	19.8	89	-	15	
10	11	9	26	-	12	
11	12	10.7	78	-	10	
data diving from to tape compass backcompass depthchange ignoreall						
12	13	8.5	25	-	-2	Little passage goes uphill straight on
data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
13	14	12.3	85	-	9	
14	15	11.6	63	-	10	
data diving from to tape compass backcompass depthchange ignoreall						
15	16	12	125	-	-3.5	Low creep at 4-10 feet. Chamber goes 15' in same line
data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
16	17	14.5	-	265	6	
17	18	12.6	22	-	6	
# 18	19	11	-	-	DOWN	18 is in crack at top of "11 foot drop" (This leg duplicated in notes and now only included in file swildons2-c)

endcentreline

endsurvey